      ":question/id": "f9d1871d-30f9-5239-9032-207f008e3a87",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following matrices has a rank of $3?$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, notice that a matrix of rank $3$ must have at least $3$ columns and at least $3$ rows. \nSo, we disregard the following matrices:\n\n- $A$ since it has only $2$ rows.\n\n- $B$ since it has only $2$ rows (and only $2$ columns).\n\n- $E$ since it has only $2$ columns.\n\nAlso, the matrix must have $3$ pivot columns. As we can see, the matrix $C$ has only $2$ pivot columns. So, $\\text{rank}(C)=2.$ As we can see, the matrix $D$ has exactly $3$ pivot columns. So, $\\text{rank}(D)=3.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the matrix $D.$",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
